{"abstract":"There is mounting evidence acknowledging that embodiment is foundational to cognition. In HCI, this understanding has been incorporated in concepts like embodied interaction, bodily play, and natural user-interfaces. However, while embodied cognition suggests a strong connection between motor activity and memory, we find the design of technological systems that target this connection to be largely overlooked. Considering this, we are provided with an opportunity to extend human capabilities through augmenting motor memory. Augmentation of motor memory is now possible with the advent of new and emerging technologies including neuromodulation, electric stimulation, brain-computer interfaces, and adaptive intelligent systems. This workshop aims to explore the possibility of augmenting motor memory using these and other technologies. In doing so, we stand to benefit not only from new technologies and interactions, but also a means to further study cognition.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Patibanda, Rakesh","Semertzidis, Nathan Arthur","Scary, Michaela","Delfa, Joseph Nathan La","Andres, Josh","Baytas, Mehmet Aydin","Martin-Niedecken, Anna Lisa","Strohmeier, Paul","Fruchard, Bruno","Leigh, Sang-won","Mekler, Elisa","Nanayakkara, Suranga","Wiemeyer, Josef","Berthouze, Nadia","Kunze, Kai","Rikakis, Thanassis","Kelliher, Aisling","Warwick, Kevin","Hoven, Elise van den","Mueller, Florian 'Floyd'","Mann, Steve"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677301"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Canada","Germany","Japan","Netherlands","New Zealand","Switzerland","Turkey","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Coventry University","Darmstadt University of Technology","Eindhoven University of Technology","Georgia Institute of Technology","IBM Research Australia","Keio University","Koç University","Monash University","Royal Melbourne Institute of Technology","Saarland University","The University of Auckland","University College London","University of Technology, Sydney","University of Toronto","Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University","Zurich University of the Arts"],"keyword":["Adaptive Intelligent Systems","Brain Computer Interfaces","Embodied cognition","Human Computer Interaction","Motor Memory Augmentation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"motor memory in hci","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85090190881","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677301","identifier":[{"id":"85090190881","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-27938b97-9edc-4189-b55f-d2e0383009ef"],"keyword":["Adaptive Intelligent Systems","Brain-Computer Interfaces","Embodied Cognition","Human-Computer Interaction","Motor Memory Augmentation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BEB763EF4BFD45B13904B7280418BA70"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"monash university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Monash University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"royal melbourne institute of technology","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Royal Melbourne Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"ibm research australia","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"IBM Research Australia","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"tr","key":"koç university","loc":["Turkey","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Koç University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ch","key":"zurich university of the arts","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, No