{"abstract":"Interactive narratives offer interesting opportunities for the study of the impact of media on behavior. A growing amount of research on games advocating social change, including those focusing on interactive narratives, has highlighted their potential for attitudinal and behavioral impact. In this study, we examine the relationship between interactivity and prosocial behavior, as well as potential underlying processes. A yoked study design with 634 participants compared an interactive with a noninteractive narrative. Structural equation modeling revealed no significant differences in prosocial behavior between the interactive and noninteractive condition. However, support for the importance of appreciation for and engagement with a narrative on subsequent prosocial behavior was observed. In summary, while results shed light on processes underlying the relationship between both noninteractive and interactive narratives and prosocial behavior, they also highlight interactivity as a multifaceted concept worth examining in further detail.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Steinemann, Sharon T.","Iten, Glena Helen","Opwis, Klaus","Forde, Seamus F.","Fraßeck, Lars","Mekler, Elisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677337"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Basel"],"keyword":["Appreciation","Games for Change","Interactive narrative","Prosocial behavior","yoked design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interactive narratives affecting social change","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1027/1864-1105/a000211","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677337","identifier":[{"id":"85017579623","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cfaa2ffb-0012-4809-8bde-b532e4941894"],"keyword":["appreciation","games for change","interactive narrative","prosocial behavior","yoked design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-58313EA643BD8B3CC0AF0552CAA628DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1027/1864-1105/a000211","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"university of basel","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Basel","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sharon T.","key":"steinemannpau","last":"Steinemann","name":"Steinemann, Sharon T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Glena Helen","key":"itenpau","last":"Iten","name":"Iten, Glena Helen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus","key":"opwispau","last":"Opwis","name":"Opwis, Klaus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Seamus F.","key":"fordepau","last":"Forde","name":"Forde, Seamus F.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"fraßeckpau","last":"Fraßeck","name":"Fraßeck, Lars","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa D.","key":"meklerpau","last":"Mekler","locid":"cf6cfa0b-e3ac-4164-8de2-b956d8e23825","name":"Mekler, Elisa","name_org":"Mekler, Elisa D.","orcid":"0000-0003-0076-6703","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1027/1864-1105/a000211","issn":["21512388"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Media Psychology: Theories, Methods and Applications","pages":"54-66","status":"p","title":"Journal of Media Psychology: Theories, Methods and Applications","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cfaa2ffb-0012-4809-8bde-b532e4941894"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Interactive Narratives Affecting Social Change","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677337","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
